# Date format and timezone

Platform **Default Date Format** and the company → platform timezone hierarchy must stay authoritative for display. Do not invent new formatters or hardcode `d-m-Y` / `d M Y` / `toLocaleDateString` for calendar dates.

Full guide: [docs/architecture/date-and-timezone.md](../../docs/architecture/date-and-timezone.md)

## Frontend (React)

- **Date-only display:** `useFormatDate()` / `useDateFormat()` from `@/lib/format-date`. Never call bare `formatDisplayDate(value)` without a format in components.
- **Pure helpers:** `formatDisplayDate(value, format?)` stays pure (no `usePage`). Pass format from the hook, or rely on the layout-synced module cache only when a non-React `.ts` module cannot accept a format argument.
- **Absolute ISO datetimes on org screens:** `useCompanyTimezone()` + `formatDisplayDateTimeInTimezone` / `formatDisplayDateTime12hInTimezone` (date portion uses platform format). Do not use browser-local `formatDisplayDateTime` for company data.
- **Crew wall-clock / movement timestamps:** keep existing company-timezone helpers (`toCompanyDateTimeLocal`, movement parsing). Do not double-convert.
- **Month headers** like “October 2026” may stay locale month-year chrome; full calendar dates must use platform format.
- **Storage / `<input type="date">` / ISO props:** keep `Y-m-d`. Prefer `AppDateField` when the screen already uses it; do not mass-replace native date inputs unless the task asks.

## Backend (PHP)

- **Human dates** for Inertia `*_formatted` props, emails, PDFs, report-only exports: `PlatformDateFormatter::make()->date()` / `dateTime()`.
- **Re-importable export date columns** (employees, sea services, trainings, contracts): keep ISO `Y-m-d` so export→import cannot corrupt ambiguous `05/06/2026` values.
- **No new hardcoded** `->format('d-m-Y')` or `->format('d M Y')` for display.
- **Storage, imports, APIs, validation:** keep ISO `Y-m-d` / Carbon; do not parse platform display formats as input.
- **Business “today”, payroll periods, leave year, crew movement clocks:** `CompanyTimezone` (company first, platform fallback). Never force platform timezone onto companies that already have `companies.timezone`.
- **Absolute ISO expiry/datetimes on UI:** convert to company-local calendar day (`toCompanyDateLocal` / company TZ) before platform date formatting; do not take the UTC `YYYY-MM-DD` prefix.

## Anti-patterns

- `toLocaleDateString()` for operational calendar dates
- Bare `formatDisplayDate(iso)` in React components (skips settings unless cache was synced)
- Browser-local datetime for attendance/leave/activity ISO instants
- Rewiring crew wall-clock, payroll boundaries, or leave rollover to “browser local” or “platform timezone only”
